Description
{{citations needed|date=October 2025}}
Ulex gallii is usually {{Convert|10|to|50|cm|in|sigfig=1}} tall although it may grow up to {{Convert|2|m|ft|sigfig=1}}. The stems are modified into spines, mostly about {{Convert|1|cm|in|sigfig=1}} long, but with some regularly spaced recurved spines of about {{Convert|3|cm|in|sigfig=1}}. Like other members of the genus Ulex it has trifoliate leaves as a seedling, but later the leaves are reduced to small scales or spines. The stems are green, and almost wholly replace the leaves as the plant's functioning photosynthetic organs.
